  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "a route path is stated when it is written as the first positional argument of the routing attribute -- omega-php's reference.attribute_applied publishes call.arg0_text on the same span as reference.attribute; the named-argument spelling #[Route(path: '/x')] arrives as the text \"path: '/x'\" and is excluded by a field_prefix \"/\" guard, so such an action is stated as routed but without its URL",
      "a class-level #[Route('/prefix')] is a prefix Symfony concatenates onto every action's path; the overlay has no clause for \"not inside a method\" and no way to concatenate two values, so only the path written at the action is stated and a prefixed controller's Route key is the suffix, not the resolved URL",
      "the template a controller renders is stated only for #[Template('x.html.twig')]; $this->render('x.html.twig') arrives as omega-php call.method named render, and every one of omega-php's call templates publishes an empty fields map, so the canonical call view that its attribute template now carries does not exist on calls",
      "a Twig reference under the default templates/ root resolves to the artifact it names, via a data.file join that strips that prefix; a reference into a bundle or a custom Twig namespace (@Admin/list.html.twig, or a root added in twig.yaml) still lands in symfony:template-name:* with no artifact behind it",
      "config/routes*.yaml is read: omega-yaml publishes a definition.config_key's scalar as the field `value`, so a YAML route's path and its controller string are both readable. The controller is a fully qualified name (App\\Controller\\OrderController::show) and no Pack states which artifact declares a given FQCN, so SymfonyControllerRef is a separate key space from symfony:class:{path}:{Class} and the two cannot be joined",
      "services.yaml tags and arguments are not read: a service's tag arrives as relation.data whose enclosing definition.config_key is `tags`, and reaching the service id one container above it needs a second hop that field_equals -- which compares against one literal -- cannot express",
      "container compilation, autowiring resolution and runtime service decoration need runtime state no static fact carries"
    ]
  },
